  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking: a shelf key may work on several shelves, as ByteShelfCommon 3.0.0's ShelfKeyInfo.Grants lists. IShelfClient.DeleteKeyAsync is replaced by RemoveKeyGrantAsync, which takes the shelf from a key and deletes the key only when that was its last shelf; IShelfClient.SetKeyGrantAsync gives an existing key the shelf or changes its access there; IByteShelfClient.GetKeyGrantsAsync lists a key's shelves and IByteShelfClient.DeleteKeyAsync deletes a key from every shelf. All of these in the HTTP client and the in-memory one. CreateKeyAsync and SetKeyGrantAsync throw ArgumentException for a permission that is none of the values, before anything is sent. Needs a ByteShelf server whose keys hold grants (its migration v0014). IShelfClient and IByteShelfClient change members, so an implementation outside ByteShelfClient must follow. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/byte-shelf/blob/client-v3.0.0/ByteShelfClient/README.md",
